Reverse of an Array in Java
Reversing an array means changing the order of elements from last to first.
1. Example
Original array:
int arr[] = {10, 20, 30, 40, 50};


Reversed array:
{50, 40, 30, 20, 10}

program:

public class Main {
    public static void main(String[] args) {

        int a[] = {10, 20, 30, 40, 50};

        int left=0;
      int right=a.length-1;
      while(left<right){
        int temp=a[left];
        a[left]=a[right];
        a[right]=temp;
        left++;
        right--;
      }

        for( int i=0;i < a.length - 1; i++) {
            System.out.print(a[i]+" ");
        }
    }
}
2D Array in Java
A 2D array (Two-Dimensional Array) is an array that stores data in rows and columns, like a table or matrix.
